  "prefLabel": "Pol 205.06 Withdrawal of Action by the Director",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-11-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pol 205.06 Withdrawal of Action by the Director. The following shall apply to the withdrawal of action by the director:\n\n(a) Notwithstanding the provisions of Pol 205.03, the director or his or her designee shall meet informally at the request of the opposing party prior to any hearing on a complaint being brought by the director or his or her designee, for the purpose of narrowing the issues to be litigated or arriving at a pre-hearing settlement in which the director agrees to withdraw the complaint.\n\n(b) The results of any such conference shall be reduced to writing and signed by all parties to the action.\n\nSource. #7302, eff 6-8-00; ss by #9167, INTERIM, eff 6-3-08, EXPIRES: 11-30-08; ss and moved by #9223-A, eff 8-1-08 (from Pol 205.05)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pol100-800.html"
